4.4 SYSTEM CLOSE DOWN

.ti 3
there is a right way to close down any software system.
.ti 3
here is the right way to close down your batch station
and UNIX.

 1) If you MUST logoff from the CYBER now,
	then go to step 2
	else you may now do one of two things depending on whether
	you want to go home now or later.

	a) To go home now go to step 2
	b) To go home later
		* Stop reading cards.
		* Allow all jobs to go to the CYBER and return.
		* Allow all local jobs to run.
		* Allow all jobs to print.
	The system is now empty.

 2) Enter "B"

 3) Wait a reasonable length of time for
	"KRONOS 2.1.2 LEVEL 439."

 4) Enter STOP and wait for
	"** batch has completed"

 5) Do you wish to backup ? (ref section 5.1)

 6) Paranoids may now use ICHECK and/or DCHECK on there discs.
	If they are not OK you may continue to close
	down but call a guru as soon as possible (appendix G).

 7) Enter "CLOSEDOWN" and wait for the "finished" message.

 8) Go to power down (section 4.5).

.ig
.ul 1
..
4.5 POWER DOWN

.ti 3
you are late for your bus !!!
.ti 3
so do the following.

 1) Insert the 11/40 key in the lock
 2) Turn the key to the POWER position
 3) Press and release the WRITE PROTECT switch on all running discs
 4) Put ENABLE/HALT switch to HALT
 5) Put RUN/LOAD switches on all disc drives to LOAD
 6) Power off all peripherals
 7) Wait for the disc drives to allow you to open their doors
 8) Remove discs to safe keeping
 9) Remove the key to safe keeping
 10) DO NOT power off. Go home.

.nx 6om5.0
